: [[118, 822], [1162, 816], [1163, 846], [118, 852]]}, {"text": "contexts: \"Since\" is used to indicate the starting point of an action or event. It is used with", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[113, 864], [1199, 853], [1199, 889], [114, 900]]}, {"text": "a specific point in time or a specific event.", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[116, 911], [618, 904], [618, 934], [117, 941]]}, {"text": "Example: I have been playing soccer since 2010. (Starting from the year 2010)", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[116, 949], [1048, 940], [1048, 974], [116, 984]]}, {"text": "They have been friends since they were in kindergarten. (Starting from the time they were", "conf": 0.944, "box": [[117, 990], [1203, 980], [1203, 1017], [117, 1026]]}, {"text": "in kindergarten)", "conf": 0.875, "box": [[119, 1035], [313, 1034], [313, 1065], [119, 1066]]}, {"text": "\"For\" is used to indicate the length or duration of an action or event. It is used for a period", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[117, 1069], [1213, 1064], [1213, 1103], [117, 1108]]}, {"text": "of time.", "conf": 0.77, "box": [[121, 1121], [213, 1121], [213, 1149], [121, 1149]]}, {"text": "Example: She has been swimming for two hours. (The duration of swim.ming is two hours)", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[119, 1155], [1205, 1150], [1205, 1190], [119, 1195]]}, {"text": "We have been studying for the entire weekend. (The duration of studying is the entire", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[121, 1198], [1163, 1195], [1164, 1230], [121, 1233]]}, {"text": "weekend)", "conf": 0.88, "box": [[124, 1242], [242, 1242], [242, 1276], [124, 1276]]}, {"text": "Prepositions of Time (use of 'since' and for'):", "conf": 0.945, "box": [[160, 1313], [737, 1310], [737, 1343], [160, 1346]]}, {"text": "Sarah has been playing soccer.", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[209, 1361], [582, 1361], [582, 1391], [209, 1391]]}, {"text": "a)", "conf": 0.62, "box": [[160, 1362], [188, 1362], [188, 1389], [160, 1389]]}, {"text": "five years.", "conf": 0.829, "box": [[644, 1357], [771, 1357], [771, 1388], [644, 13